%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: descriptive analysis
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: What is the primary purpose of descriptive statistics?
    Options:
    - To make predictions about a population
    - To summarize, organize, and simplify data
    - To test hypotheses
    - To establish cause-and-effect
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a measure of central tendency?
    Options:
    - Range
    - Standard Deviation
    - Mean
    - Variance
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The most frequently occurring score in a dataset is the:'
    Options:
    - Mean
    - Median
    - Mode
    - Range
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The middle point in a dataset, when the scores are arranged in
      order, is the:'
    Options:
    - Median
    - Mean
    - Mode
    - Midrange
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which measure of central tendency is most affected by extreme scores
      (outliers)?
    Options:
    - Mean
    - Median
    - Mode
    - All are equally affected
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'In a positively skewed distribution, the relationship between
      the mean, median, and mode is typically:'
    Options:
    - Mean = Median = Mode
    - Mean > Median > Mode
    - Mode > Median > Mean
    - Median > Mean > Mode
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The appropriate measure of central tendency for nominal data (e.g.,
      eye color) is the:'
    Options:
    - Mean
    - Median
    - Mode
    - Standard Deviation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The difference between the highest and lowest scores in a dataset
      is the:'
    Options:
    - Variance
    - Standard Deviation
    - Range
    - Interquartile Range
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The average of the squared deviations from the mean is the:'
    Options:
    - Range
    - Variance
    - Standard Deviation
    - Mean Absolute Deviation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The square root of the variance is the:'
    Options:
    - Mean
    - Range
    - Standard Deviation
    - Median
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which measure of variability is least affected by extreme scores?
    Options:
    - Range
    - Variance
    - Standard Deviation
    - Interquartile Range (IQR)
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The IQR (Interquartile Range) is the difference between the:'
    Options:
    - Mean and Median
    - Third Quartile (Q3) and First Quartile (Q1)
    - Highest and Lowest scores
    - Mode and Mean
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A z-score indicates:'
    Options:
    - The mean of the dataset
    - The number of standard deviations a score is from the mean
    - The mode of the dataset
    - The range of the dataset
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A score with a z-score of 0 is:'
    Options:
    - An outlier
    - The highest score
    - Exactly equal to the mean
    - The lowest score
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A histogram is a graphical representation used for:'
    Options:
    - Displaying the frequency distribution of a continuous variable
    - Showing the relationship between two variables
    - Displaying categorical data
    - Showing parts of a whole
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A bar graph is typically used for representing data that are:'
    Options:
    - Continuous
    - Categorical (Nominal or Ordinal)
    - Skewed
    - Correlated
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A pie chart is most appropriate for showing:'
    Options:
    - The mean and standard deviation
    - The proportion of cases in each category of a nominal variable
    - The correlation between two variables
    - The change in a variable over time
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: A box plot (box-and-whisker plot) visually displays which of the
      following?
    Options:
    - The correlation coefficient
    - The median, quartiles, and potential outliers
    - The regression line
    - The probability distribution
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A distribution where the left tail is longer than the right tail
      is:'
    Options:
    - Symmetrical
    - Negatively Skewed
    - Positively Skewed
    - Bimodal
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A normal distribution is characterized by:'
    Options:
    - Being bimodal
    - Being symmetrical and bell-shaped
    - Having a mean of 0
    - Having no variability
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: The Empirical Rule states that in a normal distribution, approximately
      what percentage of data falls within one standard deviation of the mean?
    Options:
    - 0.5
    - 0.68
    - 0.95
    - 0.997
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The 5-number summary consists of:'
    Options:
    - Mean, SD, Variance, Range, Mode
    - Minimum, Q1, Median, Q3, Maximum
    - Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Mean
    - Mode, Median, Mean, Range, IQR
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: How does the median compare to the mean in a negatively skewed
      distribution?
    Options:
    - The median is greater than the mean.
    - The median is greater than the mean.
    - The median is equal to the mean.
    - The relationship cannot be determined.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Why is the standard deviation generally considered a better measure
      of variability than the range?
    Options:
    - It is easier to calculate.
    - It uses all the data points and is less affected by extreme scores than the
      range.
    - It is always smaller.
    - It can be used for categorical data.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: What is the main purpose of using a z-score?
    Options:
    - To create a graph
    - To determine a score's relative position and compare scores from different
      distributions
    - To calculate the average
    - To find the most frequent score
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: "Assertion (A):\_The mean is the balance point of a distribution.\_Reason
      (R):\_The sum of the deviations of each score from the mean is always zero."
    Options:
    - Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.
    - Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.
    - A is true but R is false.
    - A is false but R is true.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A dataset has a mean of 50 and a standard deviation of 5. A score
      of 60 has a z-score of:'
    Options:
    - 1
    - 2
    - -2
    - 10
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Contrast a "parameter" with a "statistic."
    Options:
    - They are the same.
    - A parameter describes a population; a statistic describes a sample.
    - A statistic describes a population; a parameter describes a sample.
    - Parameters are for inference, statistics for description.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which measure of central tendency would you report for annual income
      data, which is typically highly skewed?
    Options:
    - Median
    - Mean
    - Mode
    - Standard Deviation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: A scatter plot is used for which of the following?
    Options:
    - Displaying the relationship between two continuous variables
    - Showing the frequency of a single variable
    - Comparing means of three groups
    - Displaying categorical proportions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is the STRONGEST reason for using the standard
      deviation over the variance?
    Options:
    - It is easier to calculate.
    - It is expressed in the original units of the data, making it more interpretable.
    - It is always a smaller number.
    - It is not sensitive to outliers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A flaw in using only the range to describe data is that it:'
    Options:
    - Is too difficult to calculate.
    - Is extremely sensitive to outliers and gives no information about the distribution
      of values between the max and min.
    - Is always zero.
    - Cannot be used with the mean.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of "kurtosis" refers to the:'
    Options:
    - Skewness of a distribution
    - Peakedness or flatness of a distribution compared to a normal curve
    - Average of the distribution
    - Variability of the distribution
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'In a perfectly symmetrical, unimodal distribution:'
    Options:
    - The range is zero
    - The mean, median, and mode are all equal
    - The standard deviation is 1
    - The variance is negative
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The coefficient of variation is useful for:'
    Options:
    - Finding the mean
    - Comparing the relative variability of datasets with different units or widely
      different means
    - Calculating z-scores
    - Determining skewness
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A frequency polygon is a line graph that represents:'
    Options:
    - The mean over time
    - The frequencies of classes in a frequency distribution
    - The correlation between two variables
    - The interquartile range
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The cumulative frequency for a class interval is the:'
    Options:
    - Frequency of that interval
    - Sum of the frequencies for that class and all previous classes
    - Difference between the highest and lowest frequency
    - Average frequency
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A researcher calculates the mean of a sample. This mean is a:'
    Options:
    - Statistic
    - Parameter
    - Population
    - Constant
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The midrange is calculated as:'
    Options:
    - (Q3 - Q1)/2
    - (Maximum + Minimum) / 2
    - (Mean + Median)/2
    - (Mode + Mean)/2
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'Descriptive statistics are to "what the data looks like" as inferential
      statistics are to:'
    Options:
    - '"Making predictions or generalizations from the data"'
    - '"Summarizing the data"'
    - '"Drawing graphs"'
    - '"Calculating means"'
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'If a distribution is bimodal, the best measure of central tendency
      to report is/are the:'
    Options:
    - Mean
    - Median
    - Modes
    - Mean and Median
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The variance for a population is denoted by:'
    Options:
    - "\u03C3\xB2"
    - "s\xB2"
    - "\u03C3"
    - s
    CorrectOptionIndex: 0
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'A stem-and-leaf plot is similar to a histogram but has the advantage
      of:'
    Options:
    - Being easier to draw
    - Preserving the original raw data values
    - Showing the mean and standard deviation
    - Being used for categorical data
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The mean of a dataset is 100 and the median is 95. The distribution
      is most likely:'
    Options:
    - Symmetrical
    - Positively Skewed
    - Negatively Skewed
    - Bimodal
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is NOT a property of the standard deviation?
    Options:
    - It is the square root of the variance.
    - It is measured in the same units as the original data.
    - It can be negative.
    - It is sensitive to outliers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The purpose of a "measure of variability" is to quantify the:'
    Options:
    - Central value
    - Spread or dispersion of the data points
    - Shape of the distribution
    - Most frequent value
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: In a normal distribution, what percent of scores lie between the
      mean and a z-score of +1?
    Options:
    - 0.25
    - 0.34
    - 0.68
    - 0.95
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The most appropriate graph for showing the trend of a variable
      over time is a:'
    Options:
    - Bar chart
    - Histogram
    - Line graph
    - Pie chart
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'If every score in a dataset is multiplied by a constant, the standard
      deviation will be:'
    Options:
    - Unchanged
    - Multiplied by that constant
    - Divided by that constant
    - Increased by that constant
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate goal of descriptive analysis is to:'
    Options:
    - Prove a hypothesis
    - Provide a clear and accurate summary of the data to facilitate understanding
      and communication
    - Make inferences about a population
    - Calculate p-values
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: descriptive analysis
